1615	                "In this mode connections are only accepted from the loopback interface. "
1616	                "If you want to connect from external computers to Redis you "
1617	                "may adopt one of the following solutions: "
1618	                "1) Just disable protected mode sending the command "
1619	                "'CONFIG SET protected-mode no' from the loopback interface "
1620	                "by connecting to Redis from the same host the server is "
1621	                "running, however MAKE SURE Redis is not publicly accessible "
1622	                "from internet if you do so. Use CONFIG REWRITE to make this "
1623	                "change permanent. "
1624	                "2) Alternatively you can just disable the protected mode by "
1625	                "editing the Redis configuration file, and setting the protected "
1626	                "mode option to 'no', and then restarting the server. "
1627	                "3) If you started the server manually just for testing, restart "
1628	                "it with the '--protected-mode no' option. "
1629	                "4) Set up an authentication password for the default user. "
1630	                "NOTE: You only need to do one of the above things in order for "
1631	                "the server to start accepting connections from the outside.\r\n";
1632	            if (connWrite(c->conn,err,strlen(err)) == -1) {
1633	                /* Nothing to do, Just to avoid the warning... */
